WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.000
A client agent sends a program to the compiler through the gateway. Ordinary computation runs freely. Protected functions need permission.

00:10.000 --> 00:20.000
The connection owner grants a user specific language functions, such as saving to the item bank. The provider credential stays inside the broker.

00:20.000 --> 00:30.000
The gateway preflights every compiler stage. Policy checks the entire chain. One denied function blocks the run before any stage executes.

00:30.000 --> 00:40.000
Policy issues the compiler a capability: single use, valid for sixty seconds at most, bound to the function and exact arguments.

00:40.000 --> 00:50.000
Broker verifies the capability and checks live permission before each effect. Active grants allow the provider call. Revoked permission blocks the next effect.

00:50.000 --> 01:00.000
Internet traffic uses the proxy: listed hosts for strict classes, public hosts for open classes. Metadata is direct. Learnosity is blocked.

01:00.000 --> 01:10.000
A durable receipt records the outcome. Retrying the same operation returns its receipt without repeating the write. The agent gets results, never credentials.
